  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Her Skills; Her Earning</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">EMAC Tanzania proposes to conduct a one year skills development program specifically tailored for 100 out of school young mothers in Morogoro municipal in Morogoro Region. The program will provide a comprehensive pathway to gainful self-employment through a structured skills development trajectory. The program will kick-start with reaffirming the interest of young mothers who shall be selected during proposal development phase followed by a ten 10-day Soft Life Skills Training covering vital aspects suchas Basic Life skills (BLS), Entrepreneurship, Financial Literacy, Gender Sensitivity, Psychosocial Aid Support, and Sexual Reproductive Health Rights.This foundational training aims at holistic personal and professional development. Subsequently, participants will engage in practical vocational skills where they will have at least one hour of theory every day in the training spanning 96 days for fashion and tailoring, 60 days for salon and beauty making using UpToDate verified curriculums adopted from Swisscontact. This approach guaranteesthat the trainers possess the necessary skills and knowledge to deliver effective training tailored to the participants&apos; needs.

The business establishment and growth process will involve close coaching on business and entrepreneurship management skills to ensurethey develop sustainable and profitable enterprises.

The post-training will support participant to have access to markets, which includes conducting market analysis and assisting young mother in reachingreliable markets for their products. Furthermore, they willreceive assistance in developing viable and user-friendly business plans that can help them secure sewing tenders from institutionssuch as schools.</narrative>
  </description>
  <participating-org role="4" type="24">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">E-MAC Tanzania is a registered Non-Governmental Organization with registration number 00NGO/00006226 under Non-Governmental Organizations Act 2002, with legal capacity to operate in Tanzania mainland and Zanzibar. Its head offices are in Arusha Region. E-MAC envisions an empowered community with sustainable well-being. Its mission is to empower marginalized communities including youth for well-being through promotion of initiatives and networking with other like-minded partners. E-MAC has field offices in Manyara region (Simanjiro district), Morogoro, Rungwe and Zanzibar. E-MAC Tanzania is headed by a board of directors which is responsible to overseethe overall functions in the organization. The organization itself is spearheaded by the executive Director who is assisted by Project Coordinator and Project Managers. The organization has several units including Project Development, Monitoring and Evaluation, Administration and Accountancy. E-MAC Tanzania has a safeguarding policy for the marginalized staffs as well as beneficiaries. The organization has put in a practice of hiring youth fresh from colleges as interns who later on are fully employed bridging the employment gap by equipping the youths with employable skills. Some of the youths are connected directly to other organizations for employment. The organisation also ensures that all its projects strive to include the marginalised including women, youth, the disabled andthe people who are denied access to economic resources.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Empowerment of Marginalized Communi</narrative>
  </participating-org>
